From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] secur32: the ciphers Windows' schannel has

schannel took GnuTLS's NORMAL ciphers, ChaCha20-Poly1305 among them, which
Windows' schannel does not offer and which has no ALG_ID: a connection that
chose it -- servers that prefer it, Opera's download servers among them --
reported cipher 0 and no MAC ("unknown algorithm 23", "unknown algorithm
200, cipher 23"), and programs that check a connection's strength refused
it. ChaCha20 is left out now; such a server gives AES-GCM, as to Windows.
The priority string's buffer grows to fit.

Test: test/tlscipher-gate.sh with test/tlscipher-probe.c (an SSPI client
to an openssl server that prefers ChaCha20; mutant SG_MUTANT_CHACHA20).
---
--- a/dlls/secur32/schannel_gnutls.c
+++ b/dlls/secur32/schannel_gnutls.c
@@ -434,7 +434,15 @@
 
 static NTSTATUS set_priority(schan_credentials *cred, gnutls_session_t session)
 {
-    char priority[128] = "NORMAL:%LATEST_RECORD_VERSION", *p;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_CHACHA20
+    /* Stained Glass OS: the ciphers Windows' schannel has -- not ChaCha20,
+     * for which there is no ALG_ID: a connection that chose it reported
+     * cipher 0 and no MAC (Opera's installer, "unknown algorithm 23"), and
+     * programs that check a connection's strength refused it */
+    char priority[256] = "NORMAL:%LATEST_RECORD_VERSION:-CHACHA20-POLY1305", *p;
+#else
+    char priority[256] = "NORMAL:%LATEST_RECORD_VERSION", *p;
+#endif
     BOOL server = !!(cred->credential_use & SECPKG_CRED_INBOUND);
     const struct protocol_priority_flag *protocols =
         server ? server_protocol_priority_flags : client_protocol_priority_flags;
